 or meetings for personal assistance, rather than technical safety or security control (takes precedence over AI and ML / Security for this personal-assistance case)"], "name": "AI Agents and Automation", "parent_shelf_id": "ai-and-ml", "path": ["AI and ML", "AI Agents and Automation"], "retired": false, "shelf_id": "ai-agents-and-automation"}, {"definition": "News and commentary on the AI industry's competitive, financial, and policy dynamics, including company rivalries, revenue and market share, government restrictions on AI companies, and market/usage economics.", "exclude": ["technical model architecture, benchmarks, or capability evaluation -\u003e AI and ML / Frontier Models", "an agent product demonstrating task execution itself -\u003e AI and ML / AI Agents and Automation", "a finished AI-generated creative artifact shown as the output -\u003e AI and ML / Generative Media", "coding-tool usage or IDE/SDK workflow steps -\u003e AI and ML / Developer Tools", "technical safety, sandboxing, prompt-injection or jailbreak defenses -\u003e AI and ML / Security", "model scaling, post-training or training pipelines as the dominant subject, with economics secondary -\u003e AI and ML / Frontier Models", "a company name or acquisition mentioned in passing while the excerpt's subject is hardware throughput or a capability with no business analysis -\u003e AI and ML"], "include": ["executive or public figure names who is winning the AI competitive race", "government policy or restriction reported as affecting an AI company's competitive position (takes precedence over AI and ML / Security, which covers technical safety and guardrails)", "commentary that a company now faces real competition in the AI market", "industry-wide analysis of usage share versus revenue capture between open and closed AI providers", "reported revenue or annual recurring revenue (ARR) figures for an AI company", "AI's effect on enterprise adoption, labour, task economics or economic growth as the subject", "AI accelerator or chip competition and its implications for chip and model companies"], "name": "AI Industry and Business", "parent_shelf_id": "ai-and-ml", "path": ["AI and ML", "AI Industry and Business"], "retired": false, "shelf_id": "ai-industry-and-business"}, {"definition": "Software engineering tooling as the subject: agent harnesses, IDE extensions, coding assistants, SDKs, and developer-focused workflows, described as products, capabilities, comparisons or workflows rather than taught.", "exclude": ["a tutorial, workshop or lecture whose purpose is to teach, even when it uses a developer tool -\u003e AI and ML / Education", "personal assistant or agent acting for a non-engineer user (speech, screen or task help) -\u003e AI and ML / AI Agents and Automation", "generic model comparison or model task-fit talk with no coding task, SDK or IDE -\u003e AI and ML", "consumer conversational chatbots", "pure theoretical ML papers without tools", "non-technical end-user products"], "include": ["coding assistants", "agent harnesses", "developer workflows", "software development SDKs", "IDE integrations", "code generation"], "name": "Developer Tools", "parent_shelf_id": "ai-and-ml", "path": ["AI and ML", "Developer Tools"], "retired": false, "shelf_id": "developer-tools"}, {"definition": "Lectures, pedagogical explanations, conceptual deep dives, tutorials, workshops and step-by-step walkthroughs whose purpose is to teach machine learning or how to build with AI, even when they use or name a specific tool, model or product.", "exclude": ["product announcements and release notes for a tool or model, with no teaching purpose -\u003e AI and ML / Developer Tools or AI and ML / Frontier Models", "marketing keynotes", "opinion pieces without pedagogical content"], "include": ["introductory lectures", "algorithm explanations", "machine learning coursework", "mathematical foundations", "step-by-step technical tutorials", "hands-on tutorial, workshop or walkthrough that builds or explains something step by step (takes precedence over AI and ML / Developer Tools and AI and ML / Frontier Models when the excerpt's purpose is to teach)", "conceptual explanation of how a technique, architecture or orchestration pattern works, with examples (takes precedence over AI and ML / Developer Tools and AI and ML / Frontier Models when the excerpt's purpose is to teach)"], "name": "Education", "parent_shelf_id": "ai-and-ml", "path": ["AI and ML", "Education"], "retired": false, "shelf_id": "education"}, {"definition": "Architectures, capability evaluations, multimodal systems, scaling behavior, and releases of frontier foundation models.", "exclude": ["a tutorial, workshop, lecture or conceptual explanation whose purpose is to teach, even when it discusses a specific model, architecture or capability evaluation -\u003e AI and ML / Education", "generic talk that different models suit different tasks, with no architecture, evaluation or release -\u003e AI and ML", "enterprise adoption, labour or task economics, or accelerator competition as the dominant subject -\u003e AI and ML / AI Industry and Business", "routine fine-tuning on niche tasks", "end-user application tutorials", "general AI business news"], "include": ["foundation model architectures", "multimodal model releases", "scaling laws", "model capabilities benchmarks", "open weights models", "model scaling, post-training and training-pipeline discussion as the dominant subject (takes precedence over AI and ML / AI Industry and Business when economics is secondary)"], "name": "Frontier Models", "parent_shelf_id": "ai-and-ml", "path": ["AI and ML", "Frontier Models"], "retired": false, "shelf_id": "frontier-models"}, {"definition": "AI systems and products whose demonstrated output is a finished visual creative artifact -- animation, film, or image/video-generated website -- produced from prompts or automated pipelines.", "exclude": ["release coverage whose excerpt centers on architecture,